    "text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the total number of such 5-digit numbers:**\n\n   Since we have 5 distinct digits and we are forming 5-digit numbers using each digit exactly once, the total number of such numbers is given by the number of permutations of 5 distinct digits:\n   \\[\n   5! = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the contribution of each digit to the sum of all 5-digit numbers:**\n\n   Each digit will appear in each decimal place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) the same number of times. To find this number, we note that for each place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands), each digit must appear in exactly:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{120}{5} = 24 \\text{ times}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the digits:**\n\n   The sum of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the contribution of each digit to the sum of all 5-digit numbers:**\n\n   For each place value (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands), the contribution of a digit \\(d\\) is:\n   \\[\n   d \\times 24 \\times \\text{(place value)}\n   \\]\n\n   - **Units place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 10 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 10000 = 24(1 + 30 + 500 + 7000 + 80000) = 24 \\times 87531 = 2100744\n     \\]\n\n   - **Tens place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 10 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 100000 = 240(1 + 30 + 500 + 7000 + 80000) = 240 \\times 87531 = 20907240\n     \\]\n\n   - **Hundreds place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 100 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 = 2400(1 + 30 + 500 + 7000 + 80000) = 2400 \\times 87531 = 209072400\n     \\]\n\n   - **Thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 1000 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 + 8 \\times 24 \\times 10000000 = 24000(1 + 30 + 500 + 7000 + 80000) = 24000 \\times 87531 = 2090724000\n     \\]\n\n   - **Ten-thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     1 \\times 24 \\times 10000 + 3 \\times 24 \\times 100000 + 5 \\times 24 \\times 1000000 + 7 \\times 24 \\times 10000000 + ",
